    "answer": {
      "short": "$P(x)=\\dfrac34(x-1)^2(x+2)^2$.",
      "worked": "The two double zeroes give $P(x)=k(x-1)^2(x+2)^2$. Using the $y$-intercept,\n$$\\begin{align*}P(0)&=k(0-1)^2(0+2)^2\\\\3&=4k\\\\k&=\\frac34.\\end{align*}$$\nHence $P(x)=\\dfrac34(x-1)^2(x+2)^2$. Its leading coefficient is positive, so $P(x)\\to\\infty$ as $x\\to\\infty$, as required.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
